From: ImmortalWrt Developer <developer@immortalwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: increase MT7988 QDMA TX queues to 64

Raise the MT7988 SoC QDMA TX queue count from 32 to 64 on top of
the official per-SoC queue count and register paging support, enabling
full 64-queue hardware QoS rate limiting on MediaTek Filogic 880.

Signed-off-by: ImmortalWrt Developer <developer@immortalwrt.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -7838,7 +7838,7 @@ static const struct mtk_soc_data mt7988_
 	.required_clks = MT7988_CLKS_BITMAP,
 	.required_pctl = false,
 	.version = 3,
-	.num_tx_queues = 32,
+	.num_tx_queues = 64,
 	.offload_version = 2,
 	.ppe_num = 3,
 	.hash_offset = 4,
